          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On November 27, 2015, around 3:00 PM, a driver traveling on a communal road between Noeux-les-Mines (62) and Mazingarbe (62) observed about a dozen white glowing points and a dark point moving in a cloudy sky. The driver stopped to film the event. The points moved at high speed and disappeared into the clouds. No sound was heard. The observation lasted about a minute. No other testimonies were collected. The movements in all directions of a dozen white glowing points in the sky do not have an explanation at this stage. The witness's video shows a short trajectory of a white point (at 0.24 seconds) and a black point (at 0.33 seconds). The photo also shows a white point, all against a gray cloud background. However, beyond these details, the observation information is vague. In particular, the witness does not provide the exact location of the observation, does not identify on the video the multiple events he saw, which does not allow them to be found on this video. Given these few elements, the possibility of birds is not excluded. The low level of information does not allow for the processing of this observation. The GEIPAN classifies the file in category C.",
